Subject: [PATCH] screencast: reuse the source of a restored session closed before Start

Applies on top of 0001-screencast-restore-window-sessions.patch.

Chromium-based apps restore a session with the token returned by the
previous Start, and a token is single use. When Vesktop switches the shared
source while streaming ("change stream"), it restores the new source three
times; the third restored session is closed before Start, so no new token is
issued, and the very next request comes without restore_data: the chooser
runs again for the source that was just picked (cancelling it ends the
stream; picking another source streams that one instead).

Remember the target of a restored session that is closed before Start and
reuse it for the next SelectSources of the same app that comes without
restore_data (if the output/window still exists; otherwise the chooser runs).
Forget it when a started session of that app is closed (the stream ended) or
when the app sends its own restore_data. No timing involved.
---
diff --git a/include/screencast.h b/include/screencast.h
--- a/include/screencast.h
+++ b/include/screencast.h
@@ -3,7 +3,10 @@
 
 #include "screencast_common.h"
 
+struct xdpw_session;
+
 void xdpw_screencast_instance_destroy(struct xdpw_screencast_instance *cast);
+void xdpw_screencast_session_closing(struct xdpw_session *sess);
 void xdpw_screencast_instance_teardown(struct xdpw_screencast_instance *cast);
 
 #endif
